# Resume -Analyzer
This project evaluates a candidate's resume against a job description (JD) using semantic comparison. The evaluation is done based on multiple factors, including skills, education, experience, and job role alignment. The comparison leverages a language model from HuggingFace for semantic understanding, and uses ChromaDB to manage job descriptions and resumes.

Overview
The goal of this project is to assess the alignment between a job description and a candidate's resume. The evaluation involves parsing the job description and resume into structured fields such as Skills, Education, Job Role, and Experience. These are then compared for semantic relevance using a state-of-the-art language model (LLM) from HuggingFace.
The result of this evaluation is output as a structured JSON file that shows match percentages between the resume and JD, as well as an overall score.

Features 
Semantic Evaluation: Evaluates resumes based on meaning, not exact matches of keywords.Field-Based Comparison: Compares individual fields such as Skills, Education, Job Role, and Experience.ChromaDB Integration: Manages and queries job descriptions and resumes stored in ChromaDB.HuggingFace LLM: Uses the Llama model for semantic understanding of the resume and job description.

/resume_jd_comparison
├── Extraction
│   ├── resume.py         # Extracts relevant data from resumes (parsing, cleaning, etc.)
│   ├── resume.json       # Sample JSON file containing parsed resume data
│   ├── jd.py             # Extracts relevant data from job descriptions
│   └── jd.json           # Sample JSON file containing parsed job description data
├── Embedding
│   ├── resume.py         # Handles embedding and storing resumes in ChromaDB
│   ├── chroma_db_resume  # Directory for ChromaDB instance for storing resumes
│   ├── jd.py             # Handles embedding and storing job descriptions in ChromaDB
│   └── chroma_db_jd      # Directory for ChromaDB instance for storing job descriptions
├── LLM
│   └── compare.py        # Main logic to compare resumes against job descriptions using LLM
├── main.py               # Entry point for the application that triggers the comparison



Usage
Running the Evaluation
To evaluate resumes against job descriptions, run the following command:
                                                                        python main.py

The script will:
Load the job description and resume data from ChromaDB.
Compare them based on structured fields (Skills, Education, Experience, Job Role).
Query the HuggingFace LLM for semantic evaluation.
Output the results as a structured JSON.
[
